 - Theme switching currently selects between `MainStyle`, `SKMainStyle`, and `SKLogInStyle`.
-- `CreateNewCustomerDataView`, `CreateNewSubCustomerDataView`, and `ManualAddressSearch` use TierraCeroCustomUI headers/controls and scoped crystal surfaces. `addToDom` automatically chooses the glass host for these customer/address views, `SearchCustomerView`, and `CreateNewCusomerView` when the caller uses the standard presentation; explicit interactive/glass presentations remain supported.
+- `CreateNewCustomerDataView`, `CreateNewSubCustomerDataView`, and `ManualAddressSearch` use TierraCeroCustomUI headers/controls and scoped crystal surfaces. `addToDom` automatically chooses the glass host for these customer/address views, `SearchCustomerView`, `SearchSubCustomerView`, and `CreateNewCusomerView` when the caller uses the standard presentation; explicit interactive/glass presentations remain supported.
+- `SearchSubCustomerView` scopes API searches to its injected `CustAcctSearch` parent. One match is selected directly; multiple matches appear as keyboard-selectable cards. A successful empty search opens `CreateNewCusomerView`, then passes the selected account type and search term to `CreateNewSubCustomerDataView` using the same parent. Failures report an error, removed-view responses are ignored, and existing/created results return a single parent-validated `CustSubAcct`.
 - `CreateNewSubCustomerDataView` receives a `CustAcctSearch` parent and displays every `CustSubAcctComponents.CreateRequest` field. Its address loader populates editable postal-address fields and optional coordinates; postal-only selection clears previously selected coordinates. It returns the server-created `CustSubAcct` after a successful create response, without introducing a global subaccount cache.
 - `ManualAddressSearch` uses `VPopUp`/`VTitle` for address, coordinate, and geocoder-choice dialogs. Coordinate choices display their printable addresses, and coordinate results are returned directly from the geocoder snapshot so postal-code listeners cannot clear the returned address.
 - `Sources/Service/skyline/js/visualPerformance.js` exposes the derived performance mode as `data-tc-performance-mode` on the document root. In performance mode, named modal veils and glass content shells use translucent black backgrounds (65% and 85% opacity respectively) while backdrop filters remain disabled; disabling the mode restores their theme backgrounds through the CSS cascade.
